# LeakSanitizer suppressions — see issue #414.
#
# These cover known third-party library lifetime allocations that a few tests
# trigger but cannot free. Using suppressions (a narrow, documented mechanism)
# instead of `asan-skip` means the affected tests still RUN under ASAN — a new
# Yetty-owned leak still fails the gate; only these documented third-party
# families are ignored.
#
# Every entry matches a THIRD-PARTY library frame (Fontconfig / Lexbor / libcss)
# — never a Yetty wrapper function — so a leak allocated in Yetty code under one
# of these paths is NOT hidden. LSan matches each `leak:<substr>` against any
# function name in a leak's stack. Wired via LSAN_OPTIONS in `make test-asan`.
# These symbols only appear in the ypdf (Fontconfig) and ybrowser/ylexbor
# (Lexbor + libcss) tests.

# --- Fontconfig -------------------------------------------------------------
# Process-global config (FcInitLoadConfigAndFonts -> FcConfigInit) kept for the
# process lifetime by design and never FcFini()'d. Triggered by ypdf system-font
# resolution. Both init frames appear in every Fontconfig leak stack.
leak:FcConfigInit
leak:FcInitLoadConfigAndFonts

# --- libcss (CSS selection) -------------------------------------------------
# css_select_style allocates per-selection state (including the node-classes
# array the libcss node handler API gives no callback to free). This frame sits
# above every such leak, including the Yetty node-classes handler's allocation.
leak:css_select_style

# --- Lexbor (DOM + CSS engine) ----------------------------------------------
# Internal parser/DOM-CSS lifetime state Lexbor does not expose teardown for.
leak:lxb_dom_document_css_init
leak:lxb_css_
leak:lexbor_mraw
leak:lexbor_dobject
leak:lexbor_hash
leak:lexbor_array
leak:lexbor_avl
leak:lexbor_bst
leak:lexbor_str
